          "text": "The pattern indexes as a **tetragonal ordered-scheelite derivative**, with approximately:\n\n- Space group: **I-4** (No. 82)\n- \\(a = 5.2590\\) \u00c5\n- \\(c = 11.1665\\) \u00c5\n- \\(Z = 2\\) for Y\\(_2\\)TaNbO\\(_8\\)\n\nThe weak 002, 110, and 103 reflections at about 15.86\u00b0, 23.91\u00b0, and 29.37\u00b0 exclude ordinary disordered scheelite \\(I4_1/a\\). They are consistent with 1:1 Ta/Nb ordering that removes the \\(4_1\\) screw symmetry while retaining the tetragonal metric.\n\n```cif\ndata_Y2TaNbO8_ordered_scheelite\n_audit_creation_method              'Structure solution from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common               'yttrium tantalum niobate'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'Y2TaNbO8'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Y2 Nb O8 Ta'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               2\n\n_cell_length_a                       5.2590\n_cell_length_b                       5.2590\n_cell_length_c                       11.1665\n_cell_angle_alpha                    90\n_cell_angle_beta                     90\n_cell_angle_gamma                    90\n_cell_volume                         308.833\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn        6.233\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'I -4'\n_space_group_IT_number              82\n\n# Origin choice adapted to make the ordered-scheelite relationship explicit.\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-y+1/4,x+1/4,-z+1/4'\n3  '-x,-y+1/2,z'\n4  'y-1/4,-x+1/4,-z+1/4'\n5  'x+1/2,y+1/2,z+1/2'\n6  '-y+3/4,x+3/4,-z+3/4'\n7  '-x+1/2,-y+1,z+1/2'\n8  'y+1/4,-x+3/4,-z+3/4'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nY1   Y    2   0.0000   0.2500   0.6250   1.000   0.006\nY2   Y    2   0.0000   0.7500   0.8750   1.000   0.006\nNb1  Nb   2   0.0000   0.2500   0.1250   1.000   0.004\nTa1  Ta   2   0.0000   0.7500   0.3750   1.000   0.004\nO1   O    8   0.2380   0.1030   0.0445   1.000   0.010\nO2   O    8   0.1470   0.9880   0.2945   1.000   0.010\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing is:\n\n| 2\u03b8 (\u00b0) | Reflection |\n|---:|:---|\n| 15.86 | 002, ordering reflection |\n| 18.63 | 101 |\n| 23.91 | 110, ordering reflection |\n| 28.82 | 112 |\n| 29.37 | 103, ordering reflection |\n| 32.04 | 004 |\n| 34.07 | 200 |\n| 37.78 | 202 |\n| 39.11 | 211 |\n| 40.37 | 114 |\n| 43.99 | 105 |\n| 45.58 | 213 |\n| 47.46 | 204 |\n| 48.94 | 220/006 |\n| 52.82 | 301 |\n| 55.14 | 116 |\n| 56.80 | 215 |\n| 57.80 | 312 |\n| 59.70 | 224 |\n\nThe lattice and Ta/Nb ordering are strongly determined by the pattern. The oxygen coordinates are the ordered-pseudoscheelite solution and are the parameters most in need of final Rietveld refinement.",
